How many different routes are there from point $A$ to point $B$ if you can only move to the right or down along the drawn segments?

[asy]
unitsize(0.09inch);
draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle);
draw((5,0)--(5,10));
draw((0,5)--(10,5));
dot((0,10));
dot((10,0));
label("$A$",(0,10),NW);
label("$B$",(10,0),SE);
[/asy]

A cube has eight vertices (corners) and twelve edges. A segment, such as $x$, which joins two vertices not joined by an edge is called a diagonal. Segment $y$ is also a diagonal. How many diagonals does a cube have? [asy]
/* AMC8 1998 #17 Problem */
pair A=(0,48), B=(0,0), C=(48,0), D=(48,48);
pair E=(24,72), F=(24,24), G=(72,24), H=(72,72);
pen d = linetype("8 8");

draw(A--D--C--B--cycle);
draw(D--H--G--C);
draw(A--E--H);

draw(B--F--E);
draw(F--G);
draw(H--A--G, d);
label("$x$", (40, 61), N);
label("$y$", (40, 35), N);
[/asy]
